WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.069
From one tool call to a long task.

2
00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:06.232
In Studio 1 you wrote a loop that ran a few tool calls and stopped.

3
00:00:06.512 --> 00:00:17.797
Week 1 of this studio gave you the vocabulary: in Anthropic’s terms, a workflow follows code paths you wrote, while an agent lets the model direct its own process and tool use.

4
00:00:18.077 --> 00:00:22.429
This week is about what that looks like when the task takes twenty or fifty steps.

5
00:00:22.709 --> 00:00:28.043
Every agent framework you will meet runs the same cycle, and the names vary only slightly.

6
00:00:28.323 --> 00:00:34.595
The ReAct paper (Yao and colleagues, 2022) interleaved reasoning traces with actions.

7
00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:42.405
Anthropic’s post on the Claude Agent SDK describes it as gather context, take action, verify work, repeat.

8
00:00:42.685 --> 00:00:45.075
This lesson uses three words: Plan.

9
00:00:45.355 --> 00:00:51.712
The model reads the context and decides what to do next: answer, or request one or more tool calls.

10
00:00:51.992 --> 00:00:52.675
Act.

11
00:00:52.955 --> 00:00:55.088
Your code runs the requested tools.

12
00:00:55.368 --> 00:00:57.459
The model never runs anything itself.

13
00:00:57.739 --> 00:00:58.656
Observe.

14
00:00:58.936 --> 00:01:02.605
The results go back into the context, and the model decides again.

15
00:01:02.885 --> 00:01:08.432
Anthropic’s “Building effective agents” adds two points that matter more as tasks get longer.

16
00:01:08.712 --> 00:01:18.867
The agent has to get “ground truth” from the environment at each step, meaning real tool results, test output, or file contents, rather than its own assumptions.

17
00:01:19.147 --> 00:01:25.227
And it is common to add stopping conditions, such as a maximum number of iterations, to keep control.

18
00:01:25.507 --> 00:01:27.981
The code around the model is called the harness.

19
00:01:28.261 --> 00:01:37.243
It owns everything except the decision: what goes into the context, which tools exist, which calls are allowed, what gets logged, and when the loop ends.

20
00:01:37.523 --> 00:01:42.941
When an agent misbehaves, the fix is usually in the harness, so this lesson is about the harness.
